<% if Allure::Federation::Config.enabled? %>
  <p class="text-secondary">This instance shares with other Allure instances.</p>
<% else %>
  <p class="text-secondary">
    This instance does not share with other instances at the moment: everything
    you publish stays here. The rest of this page applies once its operator
    turns sharing on.
  </p>
<% end %>

<p>
  Allure instances can talk to each other. A member of another instance can
  follow you, and you can follow them, as if you were on the same server. Their
  address includes their instance: <code>@marie@allure.example.org</code>.
</p>

<h2>Following and being followed</h2>
<ul>
  <li>You follow someone from <%= link_to "People", people_path %>, by their
    address, or from their profile.</li>
  <li>Every follow request waits for approval, here and on other instances.
    You decide who follows you.</li>
  <li>Blocking an account stops everything between you, in both directions,
    and ends its follow.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Being found by name</h2>
<p>
  Name search is optional and off by default. Until you turn it on in
  <%= link_to "your profile", settings_profile_path %>, only people who type your
  full handle can find you. Once you do, a result shows only your avatar, your
  name and your handle: never your biography, your places or your activities.
</p>
<p>
  Follower and following lists are not published to the network: who follows you
  and who you follow stays private. You can remove a follower from
  <%= link_to "Accounts", people_path %>; they will no longer see your
  followers-only publications.
</p>

<h2>What other instances receive</h2>
<p>
  When you publish, each instance where someone follows you receives a
  <strong>copy</strong> of the publication — exactly the copy your publishing
  profile produced, privacy zones already applied — and keeps it to show it to
  your followers there.
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Public</strong> publications go to every instance where you have
    an accepted follower.</li>
  <li><strong>Followers</strong> publications go only to instances that this
    instance's operator has approved, and only to your accepted followers there.
    Elsewhere, your followers simply do not receive them.</li>
  <li>Comments and reactions people leave from other instances reach you here,
    and comments on your public publications are passed on to the instances
    that received them.</li>
  <li>Nothing else leaves: not your workouts, your original files, your zones,
    your private settings, or your heart-rate zones and load.</li>
</ul>

<h2>What a deletion can and cannot do</h2>
<p>
  When you delete a publication, unfollow someone, block an account or delete
  your account, this instance tells the other instances, and well-behaved ones
  delete their copy. But a copy that has left cannot be taken back by force.
</p>
<div class="alert alert-info" role="note">
  <%= t("workouts.publication.confirm.body") %>
</div>
<p>
  So the rule is simple: publish what you would be comfortable seeing kept. The
  publication delay and privacy zones are there to help.
</p>

<h2>Your address is permanent</h2>
<p>
  Other instances know you by your username on this instance. Your username
  cannot be changed, and once an account is deleted its username is never given
  to anyone else.
</p>
